# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever cloned this.
#
# The dev box is Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout — and
# `git archive` applies the same filters, so `deploy.sh` remote mode was about to ship a script
# starting `#!/bin/sh\r` to a Linux host. That fails as `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M`, and the
# blob in the repo is LF, so nothing in `git status` or `git diff` would have shown it.
#
# eol=lf, not text=auto alone: text=auto only settles what is stored, and the CR is introduced on
# the way out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only, and cmd.exe needs the CR.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch these: a filter that "normalises" a binary corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.onnx binary
*.gguf binary
